{"ts":"2026-11-18T15:05:41Z","sha":"baba1178632662f5b6e792004cd47bf6389b72ae","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"wiki/log.md","title":"wiki/log.md: the new entry is followed by a blank line, which breaks the one-line-per-entry list","severity":"low","source":"conventions","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"A blank line in the change log makes the newest entry look slightly different from the others when the page is displayed. Nothing breaks and no information is lost.","can_cu":"The effect is cosmetic only, no data is lost, and it can be fixed later by deleting one blank line at almost no cost.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-18T15:05:41Z","sha":"baba1178632662f5b6e792004cd47bf6389b72ae","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/tat-plugin-cho-cu/rang/phien.mjs","title":"precondition() swallows every read/parse error of ~/.claude/settings.json and reports it as 'no old-marketplace plugin is on'","severity":"low","source":"bugs","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"If the user's personal settings file is broken, the check stops with a message that blames the wrong cause. It never reports a false pass, so the person only loses a little time working out what is wrong.","can_cu":"The check still stops and never passes by mistake, and the user can find the problem by retrying after fixing the file, so the harm is a misleading message only.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
{"ts":"2026-11-18T15:05:41Z","sha":"baba1178632662f5b6e792004cd47bf6389b72ae","round":1,"kind":"finding","file":"_acceptance/tat-plugin-cho-cu/rang/two-way.mjs","title":"Shape 5: the coverage table claims two classes of the machine-install axis, but the two-way tests check only one member of each","severity":"medium","source":"measurement","inContract":false,"acRef":"","plain":"The self-tests for the check prove it catches one example from each group of old plugins, not every one. A narrower check that only looked at some old plugins could still go unnoticed.","can_cu":"The settings file itself is correct and the real session check on the machine still counts every plugin, so the risk is a future weaker check, and adding the missing cases later is cheap and safe.","proposal":"known-limits","khongBacBo":true,"unverified":false,"unclassified":false}
